ars from  all of your other stock sales  so you've got this ten thousand dollar  loss and only a two thousand dollar gain  well  great news you don't have to use the  full  ten thousand dollar loss in that year  you had a two thousand dollar gain  you'll take just two thousand dollars  from the ten that you lost  and you offset a two thousand dollar  gain with a two thousand dollar loss  you're at zero you pay no capital gains  and your other eight thousand dollars in  losses  can be carried over to future  years now maybe the next year you have a  really good year in stocks  and you realize seven thousand dollars  in gains well  you still have the eight thousand  dollars in loss  that you carried over you can use  another seven thousand  to offset the money you made in stocks  and again  you pay zero now that sounds reasonable  enough and it's simple enough  but that is small potatoes that's not  how trump takes advantage of it  real losses on the sale of stock  are not what donald trump is doing  donald trump is generating paper losses  with capital losses from huge hotels and  casinos so  here's an example in 1995  donald trump reported a loss of 916  million dollars on a casino  and we'll talk about how that loss was  generated  he then gets to take that 960 million  dollar loss  and offset 50 million dollars in taxes  per year  for 18 years in 2008  and 2009 donald trump declared a loss  of 1.4 billion dollars and  he extended the ability to carry these  losses forward indefinitely  in his own tax plan which was made  effective in 2018.  so trump can take that 1.4 billion loss  and just  carry it forward in definitely  offsetting future taxes  and the trick of it is that you can also  mess with how you declare these losses  so  we imagine listen i buy something for a  thousand bucks  and i sell it for 500. i really lost 500  that's a real loss of 500 with these  huge real estate transactions and  capital investments there are all sorts  of ways  that you can move around assets and mess  with the valuation of the assets i'll  get  back to that later to generate losses on  paper which didn't really happen in the  way you or i  think about losing money and you're  generating these paper losses which you  can then carry forward your average  middle class working person can't do  this  now the other tactic donald trump uses  where do you generate these losses to  carry forward  one of the ways you can do it is with  asset depreciation depreciation means  the value of an asset has gone down if i  have a car that's worth  you know fifteen thousand dollars when i  buy it and after a couple years it's  worth ten thousand dollars  that's depreciated by five thousand  dollars now with a huge real estate  portfolio  you know a hotel a casino a big office  building  you don't just buy it and deduct it as a  business expense  like i would do with like an audio cable  or you know i bought this new microphone  this year  i'm not going to depreciate this  microphone over the next however many  years it's too small of an expense  i'm just going to take it as a business  expense and deduct it right away  but with a huge hotel if you claim to  have a hotel worth 500 million dollars  and then now you claim you know the  hotel has aged the plumbing is older you  know you've got to flush the toilets 10  to 15 times as trump says  you could say the hotel was worth 500  million  it's now worth 250 million i can now  take 250 million dollars in depreciation  and reduce my taxes and this is where  the manipulations come into play  michael cohen has explained to us how  trump does this without actually  changing anything in the real world  if i can claim you know my 500 million  dollar hotel  it's really worth 600 million so what  that means is when it goes down in value  to 250  i'm not depreciating 250 million i can  now depreciate  350 million dollars and create  a loss carry forward that i can use for  the next however many years  it's all imaginary it's all merely  pushing paper  it's accounting mechanisms and we know  trump did this  the taxes prove it and michael cohen and  others have told us  donald trump for publicity purposes  or for tax purposes or for whatever  reason to get a loan  trump will inflate asset values when  it's convenient  or deflate asset values when it's  convenient these are the mechanisms  trump has used  this is how they work hopefully it's  useful to folks to understand it
 

